More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (621–630)
621. Improper Validation of API Versioning
API Version Authorization Bypass
Older API versions remain accessible without proper security checks, allowing attackers to bypass protections.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
622. Insecure Handling of Session Cookies
Session Cookie Exposure
Session cookies are transmitted without proper security flags or encryption.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
623. Improper Validation of Multi-Factor Authentication
Multi‑Factor Authentication Bypass
Attackers bypass multi-factor authentication checks during login or sensitive operations.
💰 Typical payout: $800 – $12,000
624. Insecure Handling of API Documentation Endpoints
API Documentation Exposure
Public API documentation reveals hidden endpoints or internal parameters.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
625. Improper Validation of Data Synchronization APIs
Data Sync Authorization Bypass
Attackers access synchronization endpoints to retrieve data belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
626. Insecure Handling of Application Feature Toggles
Feature Toggle Manipulation
Attackers enable disabled or premium features by modifying feature flags.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
627. Improper Validation of File Conversion Services
File Conversion Exploit
Malicious files exploit file-conversion services, potentially leading to server compromise.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
628. Insecure Handling of Database Backup Interfaces
Database Backup Exposure
Database backup interfaces expose sensitive data to unauthorized users.
💰 Typical payout: $600 – $10,000
629. Improper Validation of Message Queue APIs
Message Queue Authorization Bypass
Attackers publish or read messages from queues without proper permissions.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
630. Insecure Handling of Application Update Mechanisms
Application Update Manipulation
Attackers manipulate update channels to deliver malicious updates.
💰 Typical payout: $700 – $12,000
